      "section": "Section E",
      "marks": 4,
      "question": "<strong>Case Study:</strong> A rod of length 12 cm moves with its ends always touching the coordinate axes. Determine the equation of the locus of a point P on the rod, which is 3 cm from the end in contact with the x-axis.<br>(i) Let the ends be A on x-axis and B on y-axis. What is the relation between coordinates of A and B?<br>(ii) Find the coordinates of P in terms of parameters.<br>(iii) Find the equation of the locus of P.",
      "finalAnswer": "(i) $a^2+b^2=144$, (ii) $x=3a/4, y=b/4$, (iii) $x^2/81 + y^2/9 = 1$",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "(i) Let $A=(a, 0), B=(0, b)$. Length $AB=12$. $a^2 + b^2 = 144$.",
        "(ii) P divides AB in ratio $AP:PB = 3:9 = 1:3$.",
        "$x = \\frac{1(0) + 3(a)}{4} = \\frac{3a}{4} \\implies a = \\frac{4x}{3}$.",
        "$y = \\frac{1(b) + 3(0)}{4} = \\frac{b}{4} \\implies b = 4y$.",
        "(iii) Substitute in (i): $(\\frac{4x}{3})^2 + (4y)^2 = 144$.",
        "$\\frac{16x^2}{9} + 16y^2 = 144$. Divide by 16: $\\frac{x^2}{9} + y^2 = 9$.",
        "$\\frac{x^2}{81} + \\frac{y^2}{9} = 1$ (Ellipse)."
